{"id": "EUVD-2026-108508", "enisaUuid": "ce724ecc-3a94-300a-b1bb-4761596df54b", "description": "Memory allocation with excessive size value in the MQTT 3.1.1 compatibility adapter in AWS aws-c-mqtt before 0.16.2 might allow a remote actor to cause a denial of service of the client application.\n\n\n\nTo remediate this issue, users should upgrade to aws-c-mqtt 0.16.2 or later, or to an AWS Common Runtime or AWS IoT Device SDK release that bundles it.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T20:34:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T20:34:50", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/awslabs/aws-c-mqtt/releases/tag/v0.16.2", "https://github.com/awslabs/aws-c-mqtt/security/advisories/GHSA-g3x5-86mr-65p5", "https://aws.amazon.com/security/security-bulletins/2026-147-aws/"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-115417"], "assigner": "AMZN", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e17881ff-9c29-3247-a8a9-53a2de66424f", "product": {"name": "aws-c-mqtt", "vendor": {"name": "aws"}}, "product_version": "0.9.1 <0.16.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "44de576e-30ce-3af6-af0e-40cb5e88ab77", "vendor": {"name": "aws"}}], "isExploited": false}